# React + TypeScript

- Write React 18 functional components with hooks; never use class components.
- Export components, hooks, and utilities via named exports only.
- Type props, state, event handlers, and async returns explicitly; avoid implicit `any`.
- Prefer discriminated unions and narrow types over type assertions.
- Keep components presentational when possible; move API calls and orchestration into hooks/services.
- Avoid inline complex logic in JSX; derive values above `return` with typed helpers.
- Keep reusable UI pieces generic and strongly typed rather than duplicating near-identical variants.
